  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Forest Effect Fund</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ForestEffect is based in The Netherlands (The Hague). They envisage to make atleast 7 acquisitions in Dutch SMEs and locally established companies to facilitateexpansion strategies of these companies into DGGF-countries. The strategy of ForestEffect is based on making investments in the foodcommodities sector with the purpose of improving the sustainability of the foodvalue chain. In addition, stopping further deforestation is a key element in theirapproach. Good management and a sound business strategy are perceived asbeing value drivers. In addition, local impact should be a key aspect whilecreating jobs, transferring knowledge to the local population and to ensureproduction growth. This will be reported and monitored on an annual basis. DGGF provides a loan of EUR 4 million leveraging the EUR 4 million which theprivate shareholders invested in the fund.</narrative>
  </description>
